#{[17592186323585 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186321877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186322842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186322842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323585 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d379d752-f7ce-576e-9786-94b4166ca354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323878 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323878 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37099" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323878 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323878 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x,y)=2x-x{y}^{2}$ and $r(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i+3{t}^{2}\\,j,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323878 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1916a81-682a-57cf-b7a5-c43c18c456ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323878 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x-x{y}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x-x{y}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(2-{y}^{2})\\,i-2xy\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$ and $y=3{t}^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(2-9{t}^{4})\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+6t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((2-9{t}^{4})\\,i-6{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,i+6t\\,j) \\\\  & =(2-9{t}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+(-6{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\cdot 6t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t}-9{t}^{3}-36{t}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323883 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186323349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323883 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323883 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323883 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]$ at $t=0$ given that $∇f(x,y)=y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)\\,i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,j$ and $r(t)={e}^{2t}\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,j.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323883 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48ca6f9a-7d23-5701-9123-39d54477cf36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186323883 #edb/ref 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nIn addition, we've been given that\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)\\,i+x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,j.\n$$\n\nFirst, we substitute $x={e}^{2t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)$ into $∇f(x,y)$ to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2t}+1)\\,i+{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)(2t+1)\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\,j \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)(2t+1)\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j)\\cdot (2{e}^{2t}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\,j) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}(2t+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+4t{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}[(2t+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the above at $t=0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(0))] & =2{e}^{2(0)}((2(0)+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(0))+2(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(0)))=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357793 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357793 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357793 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "043ac664-b524-524e-aa72-bf1d30123527" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357803 #edb/ref 1080 "-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357803 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357803 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05e78089-dc3f-5261-a0b9-838d20687d0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357808 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357808 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357808 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0661fd29-a292-5ab4-b31a-2396be427221" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358147 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358147 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358147 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2c19e560-7929-538c-bcc2-9884cff52e44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358237 #edb/ref 1080 "-8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358237 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358237 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36ecb641-5c9e-59d2-9af0-e8b4b2b12cda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358256 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186358256 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921